  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "The point \\((-3, 2)\\) is rotated \\(90^\\circ\\) clockwise around the origin to point \\(B.\\) Point \\(B\\) is then reflected in the line \\(y = x\\) to point \\(C.\\) What are the coordinates of \\(C?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((-3, -2)\\)",
    "B": "\\((-2, -3)\\)",
    "C": "\\((2, -3)\\)",
    "D": "\\((2, 3)\\)",
    "E": "\\((3, 2)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The original point is \\(3\\) units left and \\(2\\) units up from the origin. A \\(90^\\circ\\) clockwise turn sends the left direction upward and the upward direction to the right. Thus the rotated point is \\(2\\) units right and \\(3\\) units up:\n\\[\nB=(2,3).\n\\]\nReflection in \\(y=x\\) exchanges the horizontal and vertical coordinates, since this diagonal mirror swaps the two coordinate directions. Therefore\n\\[\nC=(3,2),\n\\]\nchoice E.",
